# RiseVPN API — server/api/.env.example
#
# Copy this file to `server/api/.env` (or export the variables in your
# orchestration tool) and fill in the required values. The strict-required
# set is enforced at startup by internal/config/config.go::RequireEnv() —
# missing keys produce a single aggregate error and the process exits 1
# (HOTFIX-08 fail-fast pattern from Phase 1).
#
# Variable groups:
#   1. Core (Phase 1)            — JWT, DB, Redis, tunnel, scheduler tunables
#   2. Telegram recovery         — optional, ADR-006
#   3. SSO (Phase 2 AUTH-03)     — Apple + Google identity
#   4. lava.top (Phase 3 D-30)   — payment provider
#   5. Stripe                    — DEPRECATED, removed in Phase 8 HARD-01
#

# ============================================================
# 1. Core (Phase 1)
# ============================================================
PORT=3000
DATABASE_URL=postgres://vpnapp:devpassword@localhost:5432/vpnapp?sslmode=disable
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
JWT_SECRET=                                  # required — HS256 signing key (>= 32 random bytes)
TUNNEL_VLESS_UUID=                           # required — server-side VLESS user UUID
APP_DEEP_LINK=vpnapp                         # mobile deep-link scheme (vpnapp://...)
MIN_APP_VERSION=2.0.0                        # X-App-Version floor; older clients get 426

# Tunables (optional — defaults shown). Format: Go duration string (3m, 30s, 24h, ...).
# STALE_CONNECTION_AFTER=3m
# STALE_DEVICE_AFTER=720h
# LINK_CODE_TTL=5m

# ============================================================
# 2. Telegram recovery bot (ADR-006, optional)
# ============================================================
# Goroutine starts only when TELEGRAM_RECOVERY_BOT_TOKEN is non-empty.
# Admin DM on tg_restore is skipped when TELEGRAM_ADMIN_CHAT_ID is 0.
TELEGRAM_RECOVERY_BOT_TOKEN=                 # @BotFather token
TELEGRAM_RECOVERY_BOT_USERNAME=risevp_bot    # without leading @
TELEGRAM_ADMIN_CHAT_ID=0                     # numeric chat id (admin DM destination)

# ============================================================
# 3. SSO (Phase 2 AUTH-03 — D-30)
# ============================================================
# All six keys below are STRICT-REQUIRED. The two APPLE_KEY_ID / .p8
# entries are optional this phase (reserved for D-18 future
# authorizationCode exchange) — they only emit a single startup warn.
APPLE_TEAM_ID=                               # required — Apple Developer Team ID (10 chars)
APPLE_BUNDLE_ID=                             # required — iOS app bundle id (com.risevpn.app)
APPLE_SERVICE_ID=                            # required — Web Service ID (com.risevpn.web)
APPLE_KEY_ID=                                # optional — Sign in with Apple .p8 key id
APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY_P8=                        # optional — Sign in with Apple .p8 PEM contents
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID_IOS=                        # required — Google OAuth iOS client id
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID_ANDROID=                    # required — Google OAuth Android client id
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID_WEB=                        # required — Google OAuth Web client id

# ============================================================
# 4. lava.top payment provider (Phase 3 D-30, RESEARCH §13.4)
# ============================================================
# LAVA_ENV defaults to "production" when unset. The active API key is
# resolved at startup by config.Load() based on LAVA_ENV. Compound
# RequireEnv() check demands the matching key:
#   - LAVA_ENV set to production -> LAVA_API_KEY must be set
#   - LAVA_ENV set to sandbox    -> LAVA_API_KEY_SANDBOX must be set
# Any other value rejects with a startup error.
LAVA_ENV=production                          # sandbox | production (default: production when unset)
LAVA_API_KEY=                                # required for the production environment
LAVA_API_KEY_SANDBOX=                        # required when LAVA_ENV=sandbox (used by integration test)
LAVA_WEBHOOK_SECRET=                         # required — X-Api-Key on inbound webhook
LAVA_WEBHOOK_SECRET_PREVIOUS=                # optional — set only during zero-downtime secret rotation
LAVA_WEBHOOK_ALLOWED_CIDRS=158.160.60.174/32 # required — comma-separated CIDRs of lava webhook sources
LAVA_SUCCESS_URL=https://risevpn.com/pay/success  # required — passed to lava on CreateInvoice
LAVA_FAIL_URL=https://risevpn.com/pay/fail        # required — passed to lava on CreateInvoice

# ============================================================
# 5. Stripe (DEPRECATED — Phase 8 HARD-01 removes the module + env vars)
# ============================================================
# Kept here through Phase 3 so OptionalEnvWarnings() doesn't flag them
# as unknown. Zero production code paths import stripe-go after Phase 3.
STRIPE_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
STRIPE_PRICE_PREMIUM=price_PLACEHOLDER_PREMIUM
STRIPE_PRICE_ULTIMATE=price_PLACEHOLDER_ULTIMATE
